{"post": {"ID": 398, "post_title": "Social Media Post Ideas: 30 Content Marketing Ideas That Work", "post_excerpt": "Thirty content marketing ideas for social media grouped by the job each post does, with 2026 data on platforms and what people want from brands, plus a content mix and 30-day plan.", "post_author": "3", "post_date": "2025-01-10 18:26:40", "post_modified": "2026-11-15 20:09:28", "post_content_b64": ""}, "meta": {"_thumbnail_id": "552", "_yoast_wpseo_title": "Social Media Post Ideas: 30 Ideas That Work | Reinforce Lab", "_yoast_wpseo_metadesc": "Social media post ideas for business: 30 content marketing ideas by job, 2026 platform data, content pillars, a calendar template and a 30-day plan.", "rl_updated": "2026-11-16", "_rl_carried": "a:3:{s:7:\"prod_id\";i:214145;s:4:\"from\";s:66:\"https://reinforcelab.com/content-marketing-ideas-for-social-media/\";s:8:\"decision\";s:5:\"D-178\";}", "rl_type": "guide", "_yoast_wpseo_primary_category": "10", "_yoast_wpseo_focuskw": "social media post ideas", "rl_answer": "The best content marketing ideas for social media teach something useful, show how you work, prove your results, start a conversation and sometimes ask for the sale. Short video under 60 seconds is the format people say they interact with most on most networks. Use a steady mix, match it to the platform your customers use, and measure results that matter.", "rl_faqs": "What are good content marketing ideas for social media? | Teach with how-tos and answers to common questions, show behind-the-scenes work and your team, prove results with customer stories and reviews, start conversations with polls and live questions, and make clear offers now and then.\nWhat is the most popular type of social media content? | Short video under 60 seconds is the brand content people say they interact with most on TikTok, Instagram, Facebook and X in Sprout Social's 2026 survey. On LinkedIn, text posts lead.\nHow often should I post on social media? | We found no reliable independent benchmark. Pick a rhythm you can keep for three months, such as three to five posts a week on your main platform, and put quality first.\nWhat is a good mix of promotional and useful content? | Give most posts to teaching and showing, and keep selling to a minority. This is a rule of thumb, not research. Adjust after a month of your own results.\nShould I post the same content on every platform? | No. Keep the idea and change the format for each platform, for example a short video for Reels, a text post for LinkedIn and a carousel for both.\nShould my business follow social media trends? | Only when the trend fits your audience and tone, you can add something original, and the post will still make sense later. Skip trends tied to sensitive news.\nHow do I come up with content ideas consistently? | Keep an idea bank fed by customer questions, comments, support tickets and your own analytics. Plan a month at a time and reuse each idea in several formats.\nDo I have to label AI-generated content? | Labeling is a good practice. In Sprout's Q1 2026 survey, unlabeled AI-generated content was what consumers most wished brands would stop doing. Check each platform's current rules.\nDo I need to disclose sponsored posts? | Yes. The FTC's Endorsement Guides say a material connection, such as payment or free products, must be disclosed clearly and conspicuously, in the same medium as the post.\nHow do I measure social media content? | Judge each post by its job: saves and shares for teaching, replies for conversation, profile visits and clicks for proof, and clicks or sales for offers. Compare against your own recent average.\nWhat should I post on social media for my business? | Mix five kinds of posts: teach (answers and how-tos), show (behind the scenes), prove (customer stories and results), join (polls and questions) and sell (clear offers). Start with teaching and showing.\nWhat are content pillars? | Content pillars are the three to five themes you return to in your posts, such as teaching, showing, proving, joining and selling. They keep your feed focused and make planning faster.\nHow do I make a social media content calendar? | Make a table with one row per post: date, platform, pillar, idea and hook, format, call to action, owner and status. Fill four weeks, leave two open slots a week for timely posts, and review it monthly.\nWhat are good social media content ideas for small business? | Answer customer questions, show behind-the-scenes work, share real reviews, ask a simple question and make one clear offer a month. These are cheap to make and easy to repeat.\nWhat are social media content ideas for businesses? | Use five jobs: teach, show, prove, join and sell. Mix them across two or three content pillars so your feed is useful and not only promotional.", "rl_sources": "Pew Research Center: Which social media platforms are most popular (2012 to 2026) | https://www.pewresearch.org/chart/which-social-media-platforms-are-most-popular-2/\nPew Research Center: Americans' Social Media Use 2025 | https://www.pewresearch.org/internet/2025/11/20/americans-social-media-use-2025/\nSprout Social: The 2026 Social Media Content Strategy Report | https://brandfolder.sproutsocial.com/VXTUTVL1/at/pkp7t7kq3xqz54ffv2qc97q/social-media-content-strategy-report_2026.pdf\nSprout Social: Q1 2026 Pulse Survey analysis | https://media.sproutsocial.com/uploads/2026/03/Sprout-Social-Q1-2026-Pulse-Survey-Analysis.pdf\neCFR: 16 CFR 255.5, Disclosure of material connections | https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-16/chapter-I/subchapter-B/part-255/section-255.5\neCFR: 16 CFR Part 465, Rule on the Use of Consumer Reviews and Testimonials | https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-16/chapter-I/subchapter-D/part-465\nCrowell & Moring: FTC final rule on deceptive reviews and testimonials (August 2024) | https://www.crowell.com/en/insights/client-alerts/final-rule-announced-the-ftc-strengthens-its-enforcement-capacity-against-deceptive-reviews-and-testimonials\nLater: 50 social media content ideas for every industry (July 2026) | https://later.com/blog/social-media-content-ideas/\nSprout Social: 27 social media post ideas | https://sproutsocial.com/insights/social-media-ideas/", "rl_takeaways": "Use five jobs for posts: teach, show, prove, join and sell. Give each post one clear job.\nPew's June 2026 survey of US adults found 84% use YouTube, 70% Facebook, 51% Instagram, 37% TikTok and 31% LinkedIn.\nSprout Social's 2026 report of over 2,300 consumers found short video under 60 seconds is the most-engaged brand content on TikTok (60%), Instagram (52%) and Facebook (48%). On LinkedIn, text posts led at 51%. Sprout is a software vendor.\nIn Sprout's Q1 2026 pulse survey of 2,250 users, educational posts were the top request (40%), and unlabeled AI content was what people most wanted brands to stop.\nDisclose paid or free-product relationships clearly on the post, as the FTC's Endorsement Guides require.\nWe found no reliable independent benchmark for how often to post. Choose a pace you can keep for three months.\nJudge each format by its own job: saves, replies, clicks or sales, not only likes.", "rl_g_glossary": "Carousel | A post made of several swipeable images or slides.\nReel or Short | A short vertical video format on Instagram, Facebook or YouTube.\nUser-generated content | Posts made by customers about your brand, shared with permission.\nMaterial connection | A payment, free product or other link between a brand and a person who endorses it.\nContent mix | The balance of post types you publish, such as teaching, showing, proving, joining and selling.", "rl_g_cta_service": "services/marketing-automation", "rl_g_cta_head": "Want a content plan that fits your team?", "rl_g_cta_sub": "Reinforce Lab starts with a free diagnostic of your Google and AI search visibility and a 90-day plan.", "rl_g_cta_button": "Get your free diagnostic"}}